<?php
declare(strict_types=1);
function email_automation_health():void{
 $finished=(int)mail_setting('mail_cron_last_finished','0');$recent=$finished>time()-180;$last=json_decode(mail_setting('mail_worker_last_result','{}'),true)?:[];
 $queue=one("SELECT SUM(status='pending') pending,SUM(status='retry') retries,SUM(status='failed') failed,SUM(status IN ('pending','retry') AND available_at<=NOW()) ready,MIN(CASE WHEN status IN ('pending','retry') AND available_at<=NOW() THEN available_at END) oldest,MAX(sent_at) last_sent FROM email_queue");
 ?><section class="form email-automation-health"><h2>Automatic email delivery</h2><div class="notice <?=$recent?'ok':'error'?>" role="status"><strong><?=$recent?'Cron worker recently observed':'Cron worker not observed recently'?></strong><p><?=$finished?'Last completed cron run: '.esc(date('d M Y H:i:s T',$finished)).'.':'No completed cron run has been recorded yet.'?> Test emails bypass this worker. Password recovery, welcome, order and booking emails need it.</p></div>
 <p><strong><?=(int)$queue['ready']?></strong> ready to send · <?=(int)$queue['retries']?> retrying · <?=(int)$queue['failed']?> failed</p><?php if($queue['oldest']):?><p class="small muted">Oldest ready email: <?=esc(date('d M Y H:i T',strtotime($queue['oldest'])))?>.</p><?php endif;?>
 <details <?=$recent?'':'open'?>><summary>Set up cPanel Cron Jobs — required once</summary><ol><li>Open cPanel → Cron Jobs → Add New Cron Job.</li><li>Choose <strong>Once per minute</strong> (all five schedule fields are <code>*</code>).</li><li>Paste the command below, then save. It uses this server's actual application path.</li><li>Return here after a minute. The cron timestamp should update. Then request a <strong>new</strong> password-reset link using your account login email.</li></ol><label for="email-cron-command">Command</label><input id="email-cron-command" readonly value="<?=esc(email_cron_command())?>"><button type="button" class="btn" data-copy-target="email-cron-command">Copy command</button><p class="small muted">If hosting uses a different CLI PHP binary, use the PHP 8.1+ path provided by your host. Keep this job running; saving SMTP settings alone does not schedule it.</p></details>
 <form method="post" action="/admin/email/process"><?=token()?><button class="btn gold">Send up to 5 pending emails now</button></form><p class="small muted">This is a manual recovery action, not a replacement for cron. Expired or replaced reset links are skipped rather than emailed.</p>
 <?php if($last):?><p class="small muted">Last batch (<?=esc($last['origin']??'unknown')?>): <?=esc(date('d M H:i:s T',(int)($last['time']??0)))?> — <?=(int)($last['result']['sent']??0)?> accepted, <?=(int)($last['result']['failed_or_retry']??0)?> failed/retrying.</p><?php endif;?>
 <?php $error=json_decode(mail_setting('mail_last_enqueue_error','{}'),true)?:[];if($error&&($error['time']??0)>time()-86400):?><div class="notice error">An email trigger failed recently: <?=esc((string)($error['event']??'unknown'))?>. Check the hosting error log and queue schema; no credentials are displayed here.</div><?php endif;?>
 <details><summary>Recent welcome-email checks</summary><p class="small muted">“Sent” means the sender mail server accepted the message. If it is missing from the inbox, check Spam/Junk, bounce messages and cPanel Email Deliverability (SPF/DKIM/DMARC).</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Account</th><th>Welcome status</th></tr><?php foreach(all("SELECT u.email,q.status FROM users u LEFT JOIN email_queue q ON q.event_key=CONCAT('account:created:',u.id) WHERE u.role='customer' AND u.created_at>=DATE_SUB(NOW(),INTERVAL 7 DAY) ORDER BY u.id DESC LIMIT 20") as $welcome):?><tr><td><?=esc($welcome['email'])?></td><td><?=esc($welcome['status']??'No queue entry')?></td></tr><?php endforeach;?></table></div></details><details><summary>Which emails are automated?</summary><ul><li>Account welcome, password-reset link, password-change and owner email-change alerts.</li><li>Order received, verified payment, kitchen/fulfilment progress, completion, cancellation and provider-confirmed refunds.</li><li>Booking inquiry, quotation or quotation changes, and booking status changes.</li></ul><p class="small muted">Payment confirmation is triggered by verified payment data. Order cancellation does not claim that a refund was completed. Saving an unchanged order/booking does not send another notification.</p></details></section><?php
}
